@startuml
title J09-J12 records and the personal-data boundary

skinparam shadowing false
hide circle

class "LocalUserData\n(one user, no account)" as User <<owner>> {
  -- deleted by /my-data/delete --
  MyList
  Wishlist
  TrackingPeriod (with PriceObservation)
  AlertEvent, NotificationSettings
  Reminder
  BudgetSettings
}

class "SourceCatalogue\n(imported, kept)" as Source <<source>> {
  Product, RetailerListing, Offer
  AcceptedImport (retrievedAt, source URL, checksum)
}

class ShoppingListEntity
class ShoppingListItemEntity
class SavedProductEntity
class TrackingEntity
class PriceObservationEntity
class AlertEventEntity
class NotificationSettingsEntity
class ReminderEntity
class BudgetSettingsEntity
class ProductEntity
class RetailerListingEntity
class OfferEntity
class AcceptedImportEntity

User --> ShoppingListEntity
User --> ShoppingListItemEntity
User --> SavedProductEntity
User --> TrackingEntity
User --> PriceObservationEntity
User --> AlertEventEntity
User --> NotificationSettingsEntity
User --> ReminderEntity
User --> BudgetSettingsEntity
Source --> ProductEntity
Source --> RetailerListingEntity
Source --> OfferEntity
Source --> AcceptedImportEntity

ProductEntity "1" --> "*" RetailerListingEntity
TrackingEntity "1" --> "*" PriceObservationEntity

note bottom of Source
  Personal-data export includes only the
  LocalUserData side. Deleting local data
  keeps this side so comparisons still work.
end note

note right of PriceObservationEntity
  observedAt is when this app retrieved the price.
  The feed supplies no source price date, so
  /history never invents daily values.
end note
@enduml
